Interact with test runs

List, inspect, wait on, cancel, run commands in, and read the logs and core-hour
usage of Antithesis test runs.

When no subcommand is given, lists recent runs (same as `snouty runs list`).

Examples:
  snouty runs
  snouty runs list --status completed --launcher nightly
  snouty runs show <run_id>
  snouty runs wait <run_id>
  snouty runs cancel <run_id>
  snouty runs properties <run_id>
  snouty runs properties --failing <run_id>
  snouty runs properties <run_id> --name <substring> --detail
  snouty runs property <run_id> <property_id>
  snouty runs stream <run_id>
  snouty runs build-logs <run_id>
  snouty runs logs <run_id> <input_hash> [vtime]
  snouty runs events <run_id> -m <query>
  snouty runs search <run_id> 'contains({output_text: "error"})'
  snouty runs exec <run_id> <input_hash> <vtime> 'uname -a'
  snouty runs usage --rollup week

Add --json for machine-readable output. Every subcommand prints JSON in place of
its table or its rendered events:
  snouty --json runs list | jq -r .run_id

Usage: snouty runs [OPTIONS] [COMMAND]

Commands:
  list        List recent runs
  show        Show details of a specific run
  wait        Wait until a run is ready or complete
  cancel      Cancel a run that has not finished
  properties  List property results for a run
  property    Show one property of a run, by its ID
  stream      Stream a run's property changes until the run is final
  build-logs  Stream build logs for a run
  logs        Stream moment logs for a run
  exec        Execute a command in a run that is in progress
  events      Search events in a run
  search      Query events with the event-set DSL
  usage       Show the core-hours that recent runs used
  help        Print this message or the help of the given subcommand(s)

Options:
  -h, --help
          Print help (see a summary with '-h')

      --json
          Output JSON where supported (NDJSON for list/stream commands, pretty
          JSON otherwise)

      --verbose
          Log API requests to stderr (authentication tokens redacted)

      --settings <SETTINGS>
          Path to the snouty settings file (default: ./.snouty.toml; overrides
          SNOUTY_SETTINGS_PATH)

      --profile <PROFILE>
          Settings profile to select (overrides ANTITHESIS_PROFILE)
